  "summary": "A minimalist Japanese garden style using carefully arranged rocks and gravel to represent water or landscapes without actual water.",
  "description": "Karesansui gardens feature raked gravel patterns suggesting water and rocks symbolizing mountains or islands, created to aid meditation in Zen Buddhism. This aesthetic emerged as water became scarce in temple gardens, evolving into a sophisticated abstract representation of nature through symbolic arrangement.",
